# Video D, timed against the 191.56s take recorded 2026-09-12. Re-time after
# ANY change to d.tape. Find the spans with
#   ffmpeg -i d.webm -vf freezedetect=n=-60dB:d=6 -map 0:v -f null -
# and check the frames render.sh drops in workflows/d.boundaries/ — and use
# accurate seeking (`-i file -ss t`, in that order) when sampling by hand.

# The first agent's window: the work it already did, scrolling past. Wall of
# text nobody reads at 1×, but it has to be on screen long enough to register
# as "this one is finished", so ×3 rather than ×6.
speed 26.5 39.0 3

# The second agent's window: same beat, opposite state — a tree being edited
# while you watch. Same reasoning, same factor.
speed 48.0 59.0 3

# `jailbee new` from the base-branch prompt to the container being up: the
# longest dead stretch in the video by a wide margin (freezedetect: 53s of a
# completely static frame inside it).
speed 61.0 135.0 6

# The third agent starting: banner, then an empty prompt waiting. Nothing to
# read at all.
speed 145.0 164.5 6

# The action menu open under both repo groups — the one frame that says
# "dashboard" without needing play.
poster 18.0
